ou say their grandparents were "flat-out wrong"? Of course not. They were right about the dangers they faced. But their grandchildren aren't those dangers. They're the ones who survived them. Your grandparents weren't wrong about the fire. But they may not have seen as clearly the people who got burned. And I think that's the gap worth pausing on.
